---
import '@fontsource-variable/inter';
import '@fontsource-variable/jetbrains-mono';
import '../styles/global.css';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Quick start — SigPi</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="SigPi quick start: install, configure, and chat with your coding-agent harness in about two minutes."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="bg-aurora" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="bg-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <Header />

    <main class="docs">
      <h1>Quick start</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        From clone to your first conversation in about two minutes.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="hash">#</span>How it fits together</h2>
      <p>
        SigPi is a thin chain: an agent loop, tools, and a model adapter, wrapped by a
        UI-neutral session controller. Two frontends sit on top — a terminal REPL and a
        local web UI — and both consume the same progress-event stream, so they behave
        identically.
      </p>
      <div class="flow">
        <div class="flow-item"><span class="tag">src/tui · src/server</span>Frontends</div>
        <div class="flow-item"><span class="tag">src/session</span>Controller</div>
        <div class="flow-item"><span class="tag">src/agent</span>Loop</div>
        <div class="flow-item"><span class="tag">src/tools</span>Tools</div>
        <div class="flow-item"><span class="tag">src/model</span>LLM adapter</div>
      </div>

      <h2><span class="hash">#</span>Requirements</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Node.js</strong> ≥ 22.19.0</li>
        <li><strong>pnpm</strong></li>
        <li>An OpenAI-compatible model endpoint (OpenAI, Ollama, LiteLLM, …)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="hash">#</span>1. Install</h2>
      <pre data-file="terminal"><code>git clone https://github.com/xiatianliang1024gm/sigpi
cd sigpi
pnpm install</code></pre>

      <h2><span class="hash">#</span>2. Configure</h2>
      <p>
        Run <code>pnpm dev init</code>, then edit
        <code>~/.sigpi/config.toml</code> with your API key and model.
      </p>
      <pre data-file="~/.sigpi/config.toml"><code>[models.default]
base_url = "https://api.deepseek.com/v1"
api_key  = "sk-..."
name     = "deepseek-v4-flash"</code></pre>
      <p>
        SigPi works with any provider that speaks the OpenAI chat completions API —
        OpenAI, Ollama, LiteLLM, and more. Override per project with
        <code>.sigpi/config.toml</code> in your repo, or via environment variables.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="hash">#</span>3. Chat in the terminal</h2>
      <pre data-file="terminal"><code>pnpm dev chat</code></pre>
      <p>
        That's it. You're talking to an agent that can read, search, edit, and run
        commands in your codebase — and whose entire loop you can read in
        <code>src/agent/</code>.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="hash">#</span>4. …or use the web UI</h2>
      <pre data-file="terminal"><code>pnpm dev serve        # then open http://127.0.0.1:7878</code></pre>
      <p>
        <code>pnpm dev serve</code> starts a local web frontend running the <em>same</em>
        agent core. Add multiple project directories, run several sessions in parallel,
        and stream each turn over SSE — all from the browser, with the same behavior you
        get in the terminal. The server binds to loopback by default and remembers your
        project folders across restarts.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <code>--host &lt;host&gt;</code> · <code>--port &lt;port&gt;</code> — bind
          address (default <code>127.0.0.1:7878</code>)
        </li>
        <li><code>--idle-ttl &lt;ms&gt;</code> — retire idle sessions after this long</li>
        <li><code>--max-sessions &lt;n&gt;</code> — cap concurrent live sessions</li>
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="hash">#</span>Resume a session</h2>
      <pre data-file="terminal"><code>pnpm dev chat --session &lt;id&gt;</code></pre>
      <p>
        Every conversation is persisted and can be picked up later. In the web UI,
        sessions are listed per project directory and reopened from the sidebar.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="hash">#</span>Useful commands</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><code>pnpm dev session new --title "fix login bug"</code></li>
        <li><code>pnpm dev session list</code></li>
        <li>
          <code>pnpm dev serve [--host &lt;host&gt;] [--port &lt;port&gt;]</code> — start
          the web UI
        </li>
        <li>
          Inside chat: <code>/compact</code>, <code>/model</code>,
          <code>/resume</code>, <code>/new</code>, <code>/tasks</code>,
          <code>/skill</code>, <code>/exit</code>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="hash">#</span>Skills</h2>
      <p>
        Drop a <code>SKILL.md</code> into <code>.sigpi/skills/</code> — the agent
        loads it automatically. Follows the
        <a href="https://agentskills.io/specification">Agent Skills spec</a>.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="hash">#</span>Start reading</h2>
      <p>
        When you are ready to go deeper, open
        <code>AGENTS.md</code> for the entry points, then
        <code>CONTEXT-MAP.md</code> for the project's vocabulary — the guided tour
        takes about an afternoon.
      </p>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
